DimensionDiver: Hailing from another dimension, these divers open fire on any potential threats.
RiftShark: The rift at the Sunken Ship's heart has polluted the nearby seas; causing the marine life to take on new, eldritch forms.
Cthulhu: Now reawakened, Cthulhu seeks only to begin its war anew, and wreath the world in cosmic calamity.
DeityBrain: Shaped to resemble the brain Cthulhu lost centuries ago, Lu'Kthu shall lead Cthulhu's legions to victory in its new war.
EyeOfAzathoth: Gifted to Cthulhu by an even greater deity, these eyes are commanded by Lu'Kthu to aid its master.
DeityEater: Shaped to resemble the spine Cthulhu lost centuries ago, Crom Cruach shall devourer any who dare impede its master's mission.
DeityEye: Shaped to resemble the eye Cthulhu lost centuries ago, Cyaegha shall burn away all who stand against its master with the Flames of Agony.
DeityLeviathan: Shaped to resemble a sea-beast Cthulhu witnessed in its slumber, Vile-Oct is the most powerful of Cthulhu's servants; unleashed on those who might pose a threat.
DeityRose: Shaped as a mockery of the Dryads' guardian, Ei'lor can ensnare any deemed a threat by its master.
ShadowUrchin: Deployed by Ei'lor, these urchins aid in supressing any potential threats to its master.
DeitySkull: Shaped to resemble the bones Cthulhu lost centuries ago, Rhan-Tegoth ...
DeityDragon: The Wyverns and Dragons were the first to face the twin deities. As the first to fall, many of their souls were turned into mindless servants while the rest were left to linger in the atmosphere.
RiftVision: Living curses wrought forth by powerful deity, they offer only doom to those who witness them.
SoulOfCthulhu: After being defeated centuries ago, Cthulhu's soul fled to the seas, causing a great typhoon which swallowed up a nearby ship. Its soul became bound to the vessel's wheel where it began its slumber.
Squid: The rift at the Sunken Ship's heart has polluted the nearby seas; causing the marine life to take on new, eldritch forms.
